12. Responsible AI Usage & Ownership Statement
AI tools were used as implementation accelerators and consistency aids, particularly for
boilerplate generation and validation. All architectural decisions, governance mechanisms,
constraints, and final implementations were human-directed, verified, and owned.
Earlier prompt-only approaches were evaluated and intentionally rejected due to their inability to
provide deterministic enforcement, auditability, and parallel safety. The final system reflects
deliberate human judgment in designing guardrails that constrain AI behavior rather than
trusting it implicitly.
I take full responsibility for the correctness, scope enforcement, and operational behavior of the
delivered system.

